        "date": "2026-11-22T03:05:06Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(motion): multi-axis deburr kernel - tilted cone flank on the chamfer plane, holder tilt-away\n\nShare the 3D Deburr's exposed-edge scan (deburr_scan) and pose a\ntilted cone per edge stretch: Axis5 leans about the chamfer normal\ninside max tilt, Axis4 keeps the rotary plane; the shank test picks\nthe clear pose nearest the last one, or the edge follows the\nunreachable-edge policy.\n\nRefs #1894\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
